al Reserve Board of Governors, Flow of Funds Table L.209.\\n4 Includes commercial banks, savings institutions, and credit unions.\\n5 Source: \\\"Monthly Statement of the Public Debt of the United States.\\\" Current accrual value.\\n6 Includes U.S. Treasury securities held by the Federal Employees Retirement System Thrift Savings Plan \\\"G Fund.\\\"\\n7 Includes money market mutual funds, mutual funds, and closed-end investment companies.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [792, 1751, 1452, 1905], \"page_id\": 57}], \"content\": \"8 Source: Federal Reserve Board Treasury International Capital Survey. Includes nonmarketable foreign series Treasury securities and Treasury deposit funds. Excludes Treasury securities held under repurchase agreements in custody accounts at the Federal Reserve Bank of New York. Estimates reflect the 1984 benchmark to December 1989, the 1989 benchmark to December 1994, and the 1994 benchmark to March 2000. The March 2000 benchmark was released in 2002.\\na Includes individuals, Government-sponsored enterprises, brokers and dealers, bank personal trusts and estates, corporate and non-corporate businesses, and other investors.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [798, 1914, 1452, 1975], \"page_id\": 57}], \"content\": \"Note.\\u2014Ownership data were revised (in June 1999) back to March 1989 in order to update ownership categories and to incorporate greater reliance on Flow of Funds data of the Federal Reserve Board.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 99, 171, 123], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"54\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [536, 212, 1089, 243], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Market Yields\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 269, 794, 358], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"The table and chart in this section presents yields on Treasury marketable securities for maturities ranging from 1-month to 20-years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 370, 798, 547], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"Table MY-1 lists Treasury market bid yields at constant maturities for bills, notes, and bonds. The Treasury yield curve in the accompanying chart is based on current market bid quotations on the most actively traded Treasury securities as of 3:30 p.m. on the last business day of the calendar quarter.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [135, 561, 798, 771], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"The Treasury uses quotations obtained by the Federal Reserve Bank of New York to derive the yield curve, based on semiannual interest payments and read at constant maturity points to develop a consistent data series. The Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System publishes the Treasury constant maturity data series in its weekly Statistical Release H.15.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 269, 1486, 507], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"On July 31, 2001, Treasury expanded its constant maturity index to include a 1-month constant maturity yield, and Table MY-1 now includes a 1-month maturity beginning on that date. On February 18, 2002, Treasury discontinued the 30-year constant maturity yield. In lieu of the 30-year yield, Table MY-1 will include a 20-year maturity. Historical data for the 20-year maturity is available from the Board of Governors' Statistical Release H.15.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [829, 521, 1486, 702], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"Prior to January 2003, this section also included data on long-term Treasury, corporate and municipal yields (Table MY-2). Effective January 2003, Table MY-2 and Chart MY-B have been discontinued because Treasury no longer issues long-term bonds and no longer calculates or estimates long-term corporate rates.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [330, 867, 1280, 898], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"TABLE MY-1.\\u2014Treasury Market Bid Yields at Constant Maturities\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [634, 898, 974, 931], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"Bills, Notes, and Bonds*\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 976, 1470, 1843], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Period</th><th>1-mo. (1)</th><th>3-mo. (2)</th><th>6-mo. (3)</th><th>1-yr. (4)</th><th>2-yr. (5)</th><th>3-yr. (6)</th><th>5-yr. (7)</th><th>7-yr. (8)</th><th>10-yr. (9)</th><th>20-yr. (10)</th></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"11\\\">Monthly average:</td></tr><tr><td>2002 - Oct.</td><td>1.62</td><td>1.61</td><td>1.59</td><td>1.65</td><td>1.91</td><td>2.25</td><td>2.95</td><td>3.54</td><td>3.94</td><td>5.00</td></tr><tr><td>Nov.</td><td>1.26</td><td>1.25</td><td>1.30</td><td>1.49</td><td>1.92</td><td>2.32</td><td>3.05</td><td>3.64</td><td>4.05</td><td>5.04</td></tr><tr><td>Dec.</td><td>1.20</td><td>1.21</td><td>1.27</td><td>1.45</td><td>1.84</td><td>2.23</td><td>3.03</td><td>3.63</td><td>4.03</td><td>5.01</td></tr><tr><td>2003 - Jan.</td><td>1.17</td><td>1.19</td><td>1.22</td><td>1.36</td><td>1.74</td><td>2.18</td><td>3.05</td><td>3.60</td><td>4.05</td><td>5.02</td></tr><tr><td>Feb.</td><td>1.20</td><td>1.19</td><td>1.20</td><td>1.30</td><td>1.63</td><td>2.05</td><td>2.90</td><td>3.45</td><td>3.90</td><td>4.87</td></tr><tr><td>Mar.</td><td>1.18</td><td>1.15</td><td>1.16</td><td>1.24</td><td>1.57</td><td>1.98</td><td>2.78</td><td>3.34</td><td>3.81</td><td>4.82</td></tr><tr><td>Apr.</td><td>1.16</td><td>1.15</td><td>1.17</td><td>1.27</td><td>1.62</td><td>2.06</td><td>2.93</td><td>3.47</td><td>3.96</td><td>4.